  "description": "Recurrence-rule evaluation for .NET. Provides RecurrenceRule, an RFC 5545 iCalendar RRULE parser and occurrence enumerator (FREQ DAILY/WEEKLY/MONTHLY/YEARLY with INTERVAL, COUNT, UNTIL, WKST, and the BYMONTH/BYWEEKNO/BYYEARDAY/BYMONTHDAY/BYDAY/BYHOUR/BYMINUTE/BYSECOND/BYSETPOS parts); RecurrenceSet, which composes one or more rules with explicit RDATE additions and EXDATE exclusions; CronExpression, a Vixie-style cron parser (five-field, optional-seconds six-field, and the @yearly/@monthly/@weekly/@daily/@hourly macros); and AnchoredInterval, an instant-anchored interval recurrence (\"every 4 hours after the last completed run\") in the RFC 5545 duration grammar. Every form answers next- and previous-occurrence queries with inclusive flags over DateTime and DateTimeOffset, parses with defect-naming TryParse overloads, round-trips its canonical text, and compares by value; every answer is a pure function of the arguments — no wall clock, no machine time zone. A natural sibling of the Bodu.Globalization.Calendar notable-date engine; depends only on Bodu.Core.",
